<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Due the symmetry arising from indices <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> modulo 3, it suffices to check that for a fixed pair <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and for each <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, all edges of the form <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,k)(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},k^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,k)(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},k^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\prime}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\prime}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, are covered by the construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> edges of the form <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,0)(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,0)(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},0)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> of them are covered by <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math> while the others are covered by <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{i(j-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{i(j-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{(i-1)j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{(i-1)j}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{(i-1)(j+1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{(i-1)(j+1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{{(i+1)(j+1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{{(i+1)(j+1)}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
