<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Blowup</h3>

<div id="S2.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For integers <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,n,m,t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,n,m,t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n-2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}(n)\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}(n)\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{k}(tn)\leq tm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{k}(tn)\leq tm</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1},P_{2},\dots,P_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1},P_{2},\dots,P_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vertex set of <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1},S_{2},\dots,S_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1},S_{2},\dots,S_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the k-star-forests decomposing <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote the vertices of <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{tn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{tn}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{ab}(a\in\{1,2,\dots,n\},b\in\{1,2,\dots,t\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{ab}(a\in\{1,2,\dots,n\},b\in\{1,2,\dots,t\})</annotation></semantics></math>, and construct k-star-forests in <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{tn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{tn}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{j1},\tilde{S}_{j2},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{j1},\tilde{S}_{j2},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}</annotation></semantics></math> such that centers of <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{jb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{jb}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Q_{ib}~\big|~P_{i}~\text{is a center of}~S_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>is a center of</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Q_{ib}~\big|~P_{i}~\text{is a center of}~S_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{jb}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{jb}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text"> contains edges
<math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}Q_{ib}Q_{ub^{\prime}},~~\forall b^{\prime}\in\{1,2,\dots,t\},~\text{if }P_{i}P_{u}\in S_{j},\\
Q_{ib}Q_{ib^{\prime}},~~\forall b^{\prime}\neq b.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}Q_{ib}Q_{ub^{\prime}},~~\forall b^{\prime}\in\{1,2,\dots,t\},~\text{if }P_{i}P_{u}\in S_{j},\\
Q_{ib}Q_{ib^{\prime}},~~\forall b^{\prime}\neq b.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S2.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 2.1. ‣ 2 Decomposition into 3-star forests ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, the condition <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n-2</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees that every <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a center in some forest at least once. Thus for each <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, all edges inside <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{i}:=\{Q_{ib}|1\leq b\leq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{i}:=\{Q_{ib}|1\leq b\leq t\}</annotation></semantics></math> are covered by <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{j1},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{j1},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a center of <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, since <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{j}(1\leq j\leq m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{j}(1\leq j\leq m)</annotation></semantics></math> cover all edges in <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, edges between <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> are covered by <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{j1},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}(P_{i}P_{u}\in S_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{j1},\dots,\tilde{S}_{jt}(P_{i}P_{u}\in S_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i&lt;u\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i&lt;u\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">There might be some edges covered more than once by <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math>. In that case, one needs to delete some edges in some <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math> to make the construction a decomposition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S1.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 1.4. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.4</span></a> follows by the construction for <math id="S2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=27</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#S2.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 2.3. ‣ 2.3 Blowup ‣ 2 Decomposition into 3-star forests ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Decompostion into 4-star forests</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present constructions for decompositions of <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{2}+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{2}+2</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-star forests when <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\equiv 4(\mod 12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>mod</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\equiv 4(\mod 12)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence proving the Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 1.5. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>The construction for <math id="S3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\sqcup B\sqcup C\sqcup A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\sqcup B\sqcup C\sqcup A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vertex set of <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>16</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{16}</annotation></semantics></math> where</p>
