<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check that the star-forests constructed above cover all edges of <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>16</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{16}</annotation></semantics></math> except for those between <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, to check that all edges between <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are covered, by symmetry arising from <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> modulo 4, it suffices to check that, for fix <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{i-1,~i,~i+1,~i+2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{i-1,~i,~i+1,~i+2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, edges of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(i)C(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(i)C(j)</annotation></semantics></math> are covered. Indeed, edges of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(i)C(i-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(i)C(i-1)</annotation></semantics></math> is covered by <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{X_{i-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{X_{i-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, edges of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(i)C(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(i)C(i)</annotation></semantics></math> is covered by <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, edges of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(i)C(i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(i)C(i+1)</annotation></semantics></math> is covered by <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{X_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{X_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and edges of the form <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(i)C(i+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(i)C(i+2)</annotation></semantics></math> is covered by <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we can check that the edges inside each of <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are covered, and that the edges between <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are covered.
We omit the details here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We cannot find a symmetric way to cover edges between <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead, those edges are covered by adding edges to <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Y_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Y_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Z_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Z_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> in an asymmetric way as shown in <a href="#S3.F4" title="In 3.1 The construction for 𝑛=16 ‣ 3 Decompostion into 4-star forests ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
