<div id="S3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the number of 4-star-forests in this construction is <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10=n/2+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10=n/2+2</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm5" title="Theorem 1.5. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.5</span></a> when <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
