<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Root-hypergraphs for <math id="S3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=12m+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=12m+4</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the rest of this section we extend the construction for <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=12m+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=12m+4</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us first describe the root-hypergraphs of our constructions. We partition the vertices of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{12m+4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{12m+4}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3m+1</annotation></semantics></math> sets <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0},\dots,A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0},\dots,A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0},\dots,B_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0},\dots,B_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0},\dots,C_{m-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0},\dots,C_{m-1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that all of these sets have size four. For all <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>, we label the vertices in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}(0),~A_{i}(1),~A_{i}(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}(0),~A_{i}(1),~A_{i}(2)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}(3)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the indices in parentheses are modulo 4. We label the vertices in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly. The edges in the root hypergraphs are</p>
<table id="S3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

