<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ‘Long-distance Rule’ focuses on the edges connected pair of vertices not in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\cup A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\cup A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with ‘Long Distance’. Precisely, for <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq m-1,0\leq i\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq m-1,0\leq i\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>,
