<p id="S3.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">So far, we have covered all of the long-distance edges between <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(K_{12m+4})\setminus(A_{0}\cup A_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(K_{12m+4})\setminus(A_{0}\cup A_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have also covered some of the ‘long-distance’ edges containing vertices in <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\cup A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\cup A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. It seems complicated to check this, and one can refer to subsection <a href="#S3.SS6" title="3.6 Conclusion ‣ 3 Decompostion into 4-star forests ‣ Decomposition of Cliques into 𝑘-Star-Forests" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> to make sense of the ‘Long-distance Rule’ of our construction.</p>
