<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Boundry Rule</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To cover the remaining ‘long-distance’ edges containing vertices in <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\cup A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\cup A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add more edges into the star-forests <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Y_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Y_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s and <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Z_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Z_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>’s. For <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
let <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{Y_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{Y_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> contain the following stars:</p>
